## Goal

Every 1v1 fuzz wave reports the pool cards its passing games dealt but never played. That covers the gate and `--handicap`, which shares the gate's loop. A card counts as played when a `GameEvent::CardPlayed`, `GameEvent::TrapFired` or `GameEvent::CardAnnounced` of the game names its `def_id`, setup's events included.

- The text summary gains one line: `  coverage: N of M dealt pool cards never played (M of P pool cards dealt): <first ids>`.
- `--json` gains `"coverage": {"pool", "dealt", "played", "neverPlayed"}`, with `neverPlayed` sorted by id.
- It only reports. No seed passes or fails differently, no existing line or field changes, and no hash moves.
- One thread or many give the same result.
- The README's fuzz row says so.

